    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: `customerCode` assignment on owner creation\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline now assigns each new owner a `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (e.g. `SMI-0007`).\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`** (new) \u2014 the pipeline step that computes the code:\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n   - `NNNN` = `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits\n   - mutates the `@Val Owner` in place (the same object `BuildOwner` published).\n\n3. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignCode` step between `build` and `save` (under `govern: [ transaction ]`), so the count reflects owners that already exist and the new owner has its code set before persistence.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it (MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n\n5. **DB schemas** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `customer_code` column.\n\n**Verification:** The `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` test \u2014 which creates a \"smithers\" then a \"jones\" owner and asserts codes start with `SMI-`/`JON-` and that jones's sequence number is exactly one more than smithers's \u2014 passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nNote: since the sequence is `count-of-owners + 1` computed at creation, the numeric part is only guaranteed monotonic/unique under the single-writer, transactional flow the tests exercise; concurrent creates could produce colliding sequence numbers. The spec defines the value exactly this way, so I implemented it as specified rather than introducing a separate DB sequence.",
